  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 203 AM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nToday...Ahead of an expected cold frontal passage later this \nevening/night, scattered rain showers prevailed across the region \nearly this morning driven by a 700-850mb jet and WAA. These showers \nwere high-based and falling from a shallow saturated layer, which \nwill keep QPF amounts low of up to 0.10 inches. NBM probs indicating \nthe highest probs for 0.10 inches in 24 hrs is 30-45% for locations \nmainly north of Highway 29. The showers will exit to the east by mid-\nmorning. Following the showers, a tightening surface pressure \ngradient ahead of the cold front will result in gusty \nsouth/southwest winds at the surface. Forecast soundings indicate \nmixing to at least 925mb where winds of 25-30kts look to mix to the \nsurface, producing surface wind gusts of 30-35mph. If deeper mixing \ncan occur to 850mb, a few surface gusts up to 40 mph cannot be ruled \nout, mainly in far eastern WI. Surface winds will subside this \nevening before the cold front moves across the area from the \nnorthwest. High temperatures will be about 10 degrees above normal, \nwarming into the low to mid 70s. A few CAMs indicate pre-frontal \nisolated showers developing this evening, however the front appears \nto be moisture starved, so anticipate conditions will remain dry.\n\nRest of the Forecast...Quiet, cooler, and dry conditions are \nexpected through at least Friday as high pressure resides over the \narea. This will present result in a few chilly mornings, with the \npotential for frost development Friday morning. NBM probs for Friday \nmorning's temperatures falling below 37 degrees show values of 40-\n60% for locations mainly north of Highway 29, with some spots in \ncentral WI up to 25%. The high pressure will depart on Friday, \nallowing southerly return flow to cause temperatures to rebound into \nthe weekend with highs climbing into the mid 70s, and potentially \nupper 70s on Sunday. The next chance for precipitation is rather \nmuddled for the weekend due to a potential tropical disturbance in \nthe Gulf. However, there are some indications of rain Friday night, \nbut there is little agreement in this solution.",
